      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1895, West Brow’s community was noted for having a post office and railroad service, a rare combination for a mountain town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/ga/west-brow-xx-dade-profile.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Trenton Cumberland Presbyterian Church, once a Methodist community church, was later repurposed for the Trenton congregation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://dchsga.wordpress.com/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
